<Vertical id="hs2_reciprocal_q">
<ChoiceInput id="hs2_reciprocal">
<Markdown><![CDATA[
**Which statement best explains this reciprocal relationship?**
]]></Markdown>
  <Key value="Peer pressure may shape a person’s attitudes toward crime, while those attitudes may also influence the peer groups they choose to associate with.">Peer pressure may shape a person’s attitudes toward crime, while those attitudes may also influence the peer groups they choose to associate with.</Key>
  <Distractor value="Peer pressure may shape a person’s attitudes toward crime, but a person’s attitudes do not influence their social relationships.">Peer pressure may shape a person’s attitudes toward crime, but a person’s attitudes do not influence their social relationships.</Distractor>
  <Distractor value="A person’s attitudes toward crime may determine which peer groups they associate with, but peer groups do not influence those attitudes.">A person’s attitudes toward crime may determine which peer groups they associate with, but peer groups do not influence those attitudes.</Distractor>
  <Distractor value="Peer pressure and attitudes toward crime may both influence criminal behavior, but they do not influence one another.">Peer pressure and attitudes toward crime may both influence criminal behavior, but they do not influence one another.</Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</Vertical>

