<!-- ===== The interpretive film: a ship as a metaphor (slides 259-276) ===== -->
<Vertical id="hs2_film" title="Film draft: At the Shore">
<Markdown><![CDATA[
## *At the Shore* — early draft

*A film about strength, support, and what we lose over time.* These are stills from the draft film.
]]></Markdown>
<Image id="hs2_film_img" src="images/film_draft.jpg" alt="Twelve stills from the draft film At the Shore: a rusting ship at a dock, storms and waves, fraying ropes, strained anchor chains, water entering the dark interior, and a calm sunset" popout="fullscreen" />
</Vertical>

