<!-- ===== Revising the film to represent structural inequality (slides 278-287) ===== -->
<Vertical id="hs2_fowle_recall_q">
<ChoiceInput id="hs2_fowle_recall">
<Markdown><![CDATA[
**Which was the most accurate insight statement for the Fowle (2022) study?**
]]></Markdown>
  <Distractor value="Poverty and housing affordability challenges are the primary explanations for racial disparities in homelessness in the United States.">Poverty and housing affordability challenges are the primary explanations for racial disparities in homelessness in the United States.</Distractor>
  <Distractor value="Historical housing discrimination and segregation have contributed to higher rates of homelessness among Black, Latinx, and Native American populations.">Historical housing discrimination and segregation have contributed to higher rates of homelessness among Black, Latinx, and Native American populations.</Distractor>
  <Key value="Homelessness in the United States is shaped by structural racism embedded in housing, economic, and political systems, leading to persistent racial disparities in homelessness.">Homelessness in the United States is shaped by structural racism embedded in housing, economic, and political systems, leading to persistent racial disparities in homelessness.</Key>
  <Distractor value="Expanding access to emergency shelters and homelessness services is the most effective way to reduce racial disparities in homelessness.">Expanding access to emergency shelters and homelessness services is the most effective way to reduce racial disparities in homelessness.</Distractor>
  <Distractor value="Mental health conditions and substance use disorders are the major causes of racial disparities in homelessness across communities.">Mental health conditions and substance use disorders are the major causes of racial disparities in homelessness across communities.</Distractor>
</ChoiceInput>
</Vertical>

